From be6b427d35803ad7ed2dd33d4e133b5791a99c9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koshev-msk <kosnt.shell@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:08:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] bh: demote 'missed interrupt' message to dev_dbg

The BH thread polls the device every HZ/30 and picks up pending data
when the edge-triggered IRQ was not seen. This is handled, so there is
no reason to warn about it on every occurrence.
---
 bh.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bh.c b/bh.c
index 592fad2..5663007 100644
--- a/bh.c
+++ b/bh.c
@@ -776,7 +776,7 @@ static int xradio_bh(void *arg)
 		} else if (!status) {
 			/* check if there is data waiting but we missed the interrupt*/
 			if (xradio_bh_rx_availlen(hw_priv) > 0) {
-				dev_warn(hw_priv->pdev, "missed interrupt\n");
+				dev_dbg(hw_priv->pdev, "missed interrupt\n");
 				if(xradio_bh_exchange(hw_priv) < 0){
 					break;
 				}
-- 
2.43.0

